**What I changed**
- `src/ini.ts` — implemented `parseIni` per the algorithm: split on `/\r?\n/`, trim each line, skip blank/`;`/`#` lines, section headers validated to end with `]` (section name trimmed between brackets), first `=` splits key/value (both trimmed), double-quoted values stripped of quotes keeping the inside verbatim, later assignments overwrite. Sections are created lazily at the first key stored, so the `''` preamble and header-only sections never appear unless a key lands there. Both error cases throw `SyntaxError` with `Invalid INI on line N: ...`.
- `src/ini.test.ts` — kept the existing test byte-identical, added 11 tests covering all requested cases (a)–(g), plus empty-key `=x`, `[section] extra` throwing, and CRLF line endings.

